So I say a day is a 24‑hour period starting at 00:00 and ending at 23:59 of the same calendar date.","revised_policy":"No fisher may take more than 5 kg per trip, and the total daily catch across all fishers may not exceed 60 kg; fishing may only occur if the lake stock is above 140 kg.","revised_operationalization":"Each fisher records his catch immediately on the shared ledger after a trip. The elder reviews the ledger and the lake‑stock measurement each morning. If any fisher’s catch exceeds 5 kg or the total daily catch exceeds 60 kg, that fisher must return the excess fish to the lake and forfeit the right to fish for the next two days. If the lake stock falls below 140 kg, all fishing is suspended for the rest of the day and the elder convenes a community meeting to decide whether to resume or adjust the threshold.","reasoning":"I chose the calendar day because that is how our ledger is organized and how the elder checks the stock each morning. It avoids confusion over sunrise/sunset times and gives a clear, agreed period for the daily limit."}

